Author: Corinne Sexton <corinsexton@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Nov 13 09:16:40 2026 -0500

    Genotype features: count supplementary junction reads in the split-read AF
    
    collect_features_one_site counted a read as split-read evidence (n_af_clip,
    AF_CLIP) only through a soft-clipped (op 4) primary record. In repeats a
    junction read's primary often maps to a TE copy elsewhere, and the piece at
    the site is a supplementary clipped at the breakpoint: hard-clipped with bwa
    defaults (HG002 BAMs), soft-clipped with bwa -Y (the 1KG CRAMs). Both were
    missed. Master has the same gap (x_genotype_feature.py:233/259 test op 4
    only; 234/267 skip supplementaries).
    
    Measured at the truth-matched final calls (xTea2 0553edb): 92% of HG002
    NovaSeq calls have such reads, about 5.6 per call, none already counted as a
    soft clip. Het SR AF medians rise by 0.05-0.11 on all 8 datasets (NovaSeq
    Alu het 0.433 -> 0.542), hom by 0.00-0.02.
    
    Now a supplementary clipped within CLIP_EXACT_CLIP_SLACK of the breakpoint
    (op 4 or 5) adds to its side's AF clip count and clip-length list, once per
    read (query name + R1/R2): not again if the read is already counted as a
    soft-clipped primary at the site. Secondaries never count. Fields changed:
    n_af_clip, s_clip_lens and, when the dominant side switches, n_full_map
    (features cols 2, 3, 9 -> record fields 35, 36, 42; AF_CLIP, AF_FMAP,
    CLIP_LEN). Unchanged: raw clip counts (LRAWCLIP/RRAWCLIP), polyA tally,
    pair counts.
    
    Tests: tests/test_gntp_supp_clips.py (5 of 8 fail on the old code).
    Suite: 492 passed, 44 skipped.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017wYSUJ9R9m95ufrVRUZp1E

